  "notes": "Distinguishing features of this submission are that this has the on runout credits to correspond to the release, and is a cover variant for a release with these address labels.  NON-Gatefold Cover. \n\nPrimarily, RG for Rob Grinell, who cut the lacquers at Atlantic Studios.  plated and matrixed by Longwear Plating, the stampers were sent to Monarch Record Co and display the lowest Monarch delta numbers, Δ13712.\nAtlantic Red & Green labels with 1841 Broadway, New York, NY\n\nMO on center label are pressing codes for [l=Monarch Record Mfg. Co.]. As are the (MR) stamped in the deadwax and the delta catalog numbers, identifiers for [l=Monarch Record Mfg. Co.]., Los Angeles, CA. The delta work number, △13712 is not listed on Monarch's work list, but is between △13705 and △13713 orders processed Aug.16,1969. The release date is from BSN pubs.\n.\nRelease in non-gatefold cover and non-commercial Atlantic/ ATCO inner sleeve.\nInner Liner Photos are credited, obvious no gatefold yet.",
  "released_formatted": "Sep 1969",
